{"num":108,"nome":"Breathing Ball (Hoberman Sphere)","idade":"3–8 years","duracao":"2 to 3 minutes","materiais":"A Hoberman-style expandable sphere",
 "descricao":"The child expands the sphere while breathing in and contracts it while breathing out, visually following their own breathing rhythm.",
 "passos":["Hold the closed sphere in the child's hands (or together with them).","On the in-breath, expand the sphere together, opening it slowly.","On the out-breath, close the sphere slowly, repeating the cycle a few times."],
 "beneficio":"The concrete, three-dimensional visual support makes it much easier to understand breathing rhythm for young children or those who struggle with abstraction.",
 "dica":"If you don't have the sphere, a party balloon (not fully inflated) can be used as a similar alternative."},
{"num":109,"nome":"Follow the Thumb (H Pattern)","idade":"5–10 years","duracao":"2 to 3 minutes","materiais":"No materials needed",
 "descricao":"The child moves their own thumb tracing an H, circles and diagonals in the air, with the eyes following the movement and the head still.",
 "passos":["Have the child extend an arm forward with the thumb up.","They move the thumb slowly tracing an H in the air (up, down, sideways), keeping the head still.","Repeat tracing circles and then diagonals, always following only with the eyes."],
 "beneficio":"Trains smooth eye tracking isolated from head movement, an important foundational visual skill for following lines of text while reading.",
 "dica":"If the child moves their head along with it, gently remind them 'only your eyes move' — a few reminders are usually needed at first."},
{"num":110,"nome":"Pencil Push-Ups","idade":"6–10 years","duracao":"2 minutes","materiais":"A pencil",
 "descricao":"The child slowly brings a pencil toward their own nose, keeping visual focus on it until it almost doubles in image.",
 "passos":["Have the child hold a pencil with the arm stretched out in front of their face.","They slowly bring the pencil toward the nose, keeping their eyes focused on it the whole time.","When the image starts to double, they move the pencil back out, repeating the movement a few times."],
 "beneficio":"Trains eye convergence (the two eyes working together up close), a visual skill linked to reading and sustained attention.",
 "dica":"If the child feels discomfort or a headache, stop and try again another time with fewer reps."},
{"num":111,"nome":"Follow the Bubble","idade":"3–6 years","duracao":"3 minutes","materiais":"A bottle of bubble solution",
 "descricao":"The child follows soap bubbles with only their eyes, without turning their head, until they pop or reach the ground.",
 "passos":["Blow a bubble slowly.","Have the child follow the bubble with only their eyes, keeping their head still.","Repeat a few times, varying the direction of the bubbles."],
 "beneficio":"A playful, effortless-feeling way to train smooth visual tracking in young children, without it feeling like a formal exercise.",
 "dica":"Blow the bubbles at different heights and speeds to vary the visual challenge."},
{"num":112,"nome":"Flashlight on the Ceiling","idade":"4–8 years","duracao":"2 to 3 minutes","materiais":"A flashlight and a dim room",
 "descricao":"In a dimly lit room, the child follows the flashlight's dot of light on the ceiling or wall with their eyes.",
 "passos":["Dim the room a bit and turn on a flashlight.","Move the beam of light slowly across the ceiling or wall, in straight lines and then curves.","Have the child follow the dot of light with only their eyes, without pointing or getting up."],
 "beneficio":"A calm, engaging way to train visual tracking, especially effective at night as part of a wind-down routine before bed.",
 "dica":"Use it as part of the bedtime routine, right before lying down, to help the transition from an agitated day to sleep."},
{"num":113,"nome":"Ball in the Gutter","idade":"4–8 years","duracao":"3 minutes","materiais":"A pool-noodle half cut lengthwise and a small ball",
 "descricao":"The child rolls a small ball along a gutter (made from a pool noodle cut in half) and follows it with their eyes to the end.",
 "passos":["Cut a pool noodle in half lengthwise, forming a gutter.","Tilt the gutter slightly and release a small ball at one end.","Have the child follow the ball with their eyes until it reaches the end."],
 "beneficio":"The predictable, steady movement of the ball is ideal for training smooth visual tracking in a calm, repetitive way.",
 "dica":"Let the child release their own ball and time it — the sense of control boosts engagement in the activity."},
{"num":114,"nome":"Cards Around the 8","idade":"5–10 years","duracao":"3 minutes","materiais":"A large lazy 8 drawn on paper and a few playing cards",
 "descricao":"The child moves playing cards along the path of a drawn lazy 8, following them with their eyes.",
 "passos":["Draw a large lazy 8 on a sheet of paper or on the floor with chalk.","Have the child slowly move a card following the outline of the 8.","The eyes follow the card the whole time, without turning the head abruptly."],
 "beneficio":"Combines midline crossing with visual-tracking practice, reinforcing two skills at once in a single activity.",
 "dica":"Have the child name the card's suit or number at specific points along the 8, adding an attention challenge."},
{"num":115,"nome":"Breathing + Eye Movement","idade":"5–10 years","duracao":"2 minutes","materiais":"No materials needed",
 "descricao":"The child breathes in looking to one side and breathes out looking to the opposite side, combining breathing and smooth tracking.",
 "passos":["Have the child look left while breathing in slowly.","They look right while breathing out slowly.","Repeat the cycle 5 to 6 times, keeping the head still, only the eyes moving."],
 "beneficio":"Combines two regulating resources in one practice — the calm of breathing and the visual organization of tracking — boosting the effect of both.",
 "dica":"Go very slowly at first; if the child feels dizzy, reduce the range of eye movement."},
{"num":116,"nome":"Simon Memory (Color Sequence)","idade":"5–10 years","duracao":"5 to 10 minutes","materiais":"A Simon-style electronic game or colored cards",
 "descricao":"The child must repeat growing sequences of colors or sounds, directly training working memory.",
 "passos":["Use an electronic Simon-style game, or create a homemade version with 4 colored cards.","Show a short sequence of colors (or tap the cards in an order) and have the child repeat it.","Increase the sequence by one color each successful round."],
 "beneficio":"Repeating ever-longer sequences is one of the most direct ways to train working memory, a core executive function for following multi-step instructions.",
 "dica":"If the child makes a mistake, go back to the previous sequence length before trying to increase it again — steady success keeps motivation up."},
{"num":117,"nome":"'I Went to the Market and Bought...'","idade":"5–10 years","duracao":"5 to 10 minutes","materiais":"No materials needed",
 "descricao":"A game where each participant repeats the list of items already named and adds a new one at the end, in a growing cycle.",
 "passos":["Start by saying: 'I went to the market and bought an apple.'","The next player repeats the previous item and adds a new one: 'I went to the market and bought an apple and a banana.'","Continue the round, each person repeating the whole list and adding one more item."],
 "beneficio":"A classic verbal memory game that can be played anywhere (in line, in the car, at the dinner table) with no materials needed.",
 "dica":"Adapt the theme to the child's interests ('I went to the zoo and saw...') to keep engagement up over the 30 days."},
{"num":118,"nome":"Simon Says","idade":"3–10 years","duracao":"5 to 8 minutes","materiais":"No materials needed",
 "descricao":"The child should only follow the adult's commands when they start with the phrase 'Simon says'; commands without that phrase should be ignored.",
 "passos":["Explain the rule: only follow the command if it starts with 'Simon says.'","Give commands alternating with and without the magic phrase: 'Simon says touch your nose' / 'jump.'","Whoever follows a command without 'Simon says' learns with a laugh, no punishment, and the game continues."],
 "beneficio":"Trains attentive listening, remembering the rule, and above all, inhibiting an automatic response — the skill most often missing in children with chronic defiance.",
 "dica":"Play this regularly as preventive practice, not as a test — the goal is practicing the pause before acting, not catching the child out."},
{"num":119,"nome":"Magic Cup","idade":"4–8 years","duracao":"5 minutes","materiais":"Three opaque cups and a small ball",
 "descricao":"The adult shuffles three upside-down cups, one of them hiding a small ball, and the child tries to guess where it is.",
 "passos":["Place a small ball under one of three upside-down cups.","Shuffle the cups slowly, swapping their positions a few times.","Have the child point to where they think the ball is."],
 "beneficio":"Visually tracking a moving object among distractors trains sustained attention and visual tracking in a competitive, fun way.",
 "dica":"Start by shuffling very slowly and only a few times, increasing the difficulty only as the child gains confidence."},
{"num":120,"nome":"Telephone Game","idade":"5–10 years","duracao":"5 to 10 minutes","materiais":"No materials needed (works best in a group)",
 "descricao":"A message is whispered from person to person along a line or circle, until it reaches the last person, who says out loud what they heard.",
 "passos":["Form a line or circle with at least 3 people.","The first person whispers a short sentence into the next person's ear, who passes it on the same way.","The last person says out loud what they heard, and you compare it with the original sentence."],
 "beneficio":"Demands full auditory attention to a stimulus heard only once in a whisper, training active listening and short-term memory in a fun way.",
 "dica":"Use shorter sentences for younger children and gradually increase the complexity as the group's age and skill grow."},
